  "query_preview": "..High pressure centered over the Four Corners will\nbegin moving east later this week. A high amount of moisture sits\nover the state at this time which will lead to numerous showers\nand storms during both the day and nighttime hours. Steering flow\nthis afternoon will be off to the northwest, but as the high\nshifts further east storm motion will be towards the north or\nnortheast on Wednesday. As soils become more saturated as the week\nprogresses, flash flooding will definitely be a concern across the\nregion.\n\nBig wild card in the forecast for late this week and into the\nweekend will be an approaching trough coming in off the West\nCoast which could bring some drier air into the region. Depending\non how far south the trough digs will be the determination on \nwhether or not we get a brief break in the monsoon or no break at \nall. Compared to yesterday's model run, it looks like the trough \nmay give the area a brief pause in the monsoon on Saturday with \nonly the White Mountains seeing any good POPS. Sunday and Monday \nbrings a wetter solution with POPs returning across the Rim versus\nremaining dry like in the previous run. Will keep an eye on \nthings and see what happens.",
